## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: 3 câu hỏi phỏng vấn

**Q1. "How do you migrate production data safely?"**
> *"Back up first and verify the backup restores — that's step one, not step zero. Then write the migration script so it defaults to dry run, so you have to actively opt in to writing. Validate every row on the way through, because old data always has surprises. Make it re-runnable with upsert, so if it dies halfway you just run it again. And reconcile afterwards — not just row counts, but a sum of something numeric, because a mapping error gives you the right count with wrong values."*

**Q2. "Why cursor pagination instead of offset?"**
> *"Two reasons. Offset gets slower as you go deeper because the database reads and discards every skipped row. And it's incorrect on a list that changes — if a row is inserted while someone is scrolling, everything shifts and they see duplicates or miss items.*
> *Cursor pagination uses the last row's sort key as the starting point, so it's stable. One detail: I compare the tuple of timestamp and ID, not just the timestamp, because two meals can share a timestamp and then the ordering isn't unique."*

**Q3. "What went wrong during your migration?"**
> *[Trả lời thật với cái xảy ra hôm nay. Nếu không có gì hỏng, nói vậy — nhưng kể những dòng bị Zod chặn và bạn đã quyết định gì với chúng.]*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `dry run` | chạy thử không ghi | *It defaults to a dry run.* |
| `opt in` | chủ động chọn bật | *You have to actively opt in.* |
| `re-runnable` | chạy lại được | *Make it re-runnable with upsert.* |
| `reconcile` (v) | đối chiếu | *Reconcile afterwards.* |
| `discard` (v) | đọc rồi bỏ | *The database reads and discards skipped rows.* |

